# Cloud Agent Environment

Environment notes for Cursor Cloud agents in this repository. General
development guidance lives in the root `AGENTS.md`.

## Toolchain

Manage tool versions with `mise`: install `mise` first, then configure
dependencies as needed (from a `mise.toml` or on request). **Do not install or
change anything without explicit user authorization.**

Required CLIs: `terraform` (>= 1.0), `just`, `aws` (AWS CLI v2),
`terraform-docs`, `jq`.

## Startup / update script

The dependency-refresh step is `terraform init -input=false -upgrade` (the
environment `install` command). Keep it minimal — do not add system-dependency
installation here.

## Verifying the environment

Offline loop (no AWS credentials): `just init` -> `just validate` ->
`terraform fmt -check -recursive`.

`just plan` / `just apply` require real AWS credentials plus a pre-existing VPC,
DB subnet group, and security groups. The AWS provider validates credentials via
STS even at `plan` time, so `plan` cannot run fully offline.
